    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0601" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6193/11–1948: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-19">November 19,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–234. On behalf of another agency of the government please submit any additional
                    information not already reported concerning the recent activities of Soviet
                    Ambassador Roschin, especially in regard <pb facs="0602" n="592" xml:id="pg592"
                    /> to discussions he is reported to have held with high officials in the
                    Ministry of Defense and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of China.</p>
                <p>This request has also been addressed to the Department of the Army and Navy and
                    may have been referred by them to their representatives at Nanking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
